From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: office <office@localhost>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0500
Subject: [PATCH] wordcraft-web: shape an opened document in slices before its
 first layout

Phase 6 WP2 step 2, option (c) (docs/phase6/PLAN.md section 7, docs/phase6/m3.md): opening a large document was one main-thread task of seconds on a phone (the whole layout in the first frame; 85 % of it is shaping paragraphs). layout: `warm()` lays the body's paragraphs and tables out into the LayoutCache under the keys the first pass will look up, for about a budget per call, and returns when done; `layout()` then mostly paginates. The pass's walk-state set-up moves into `pass_ctx`/`new_ctx` so the warm-up starts from the same field context, notes hash and list counters. engine: `Session::warm_layout` with the options `layout()` uses (now built in one place, `layout_options`). wordcraft-web: after a document opens the shell runs 25 ms slices per frame (the plan's 8-10 ms lost about 60 % of the warm-up to frame overhead at 6x CPU), draws nothing meanwhile and posts `wordcraft:opened` only after the frame that shows it. Desktop apps never call it; their layout is unchanged.
